     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.8 # of global and regional policy guidance and tools launched in support of integrated risk governance &#x2013; 1</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.8 - Risk-informed Development: A Strategy Tool for Integrating Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation into Development: The draft tool was finalized in consultation with UNDP regional hubs and country offices, including the development of several detailed country case studies. This strategy tool addresses repeated calls for practical guidance on integrating both disaster and climate related risks into development, and an approach that helps overcome policy siloes and fosters joined-up implementation and localization. It is a contribution to risk-informing the 2030 Agenda and risk-proofing development investments in UNDP programme countries. The tool is a joint GPN knowledge product of the Crisis Bureau (CB) and the Bureau for Policy and Programme Support (BPPS) that was led by the DRT.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 # of countries with data-informed development and investment plans that incorporate integrated solutions to reduce disaster risks and enable climate change adaptation &#x2013; 4 (global team) 
1.4 # of countries supported with harmonized policies, legal frameworks, and more integrated institutional arrangements for DRR, CCA and development &#x2013; 4 (global team) 
1.8 # of global and regional policy guidance and tools launched in support of integrated risk governance &#x2013; 8 (global team) 
1.2 &#x2013; 1.3 &#x2013; 1.5 no targets set by global team for 2021 
1.7 implementation deferred to start of OCAPs project</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.8 = Consultations on Risk-Informed Development (RID) took place together with the Conflict Prevention, Climate Nature and Environment and Financial Sector Hub Teams, including sessions on Recovery Solutions with the Human Mobility Team and the ECIS, LAC and AP Bureau and Country Office Technical Teams and Leadership. The outcome of the consultations resulted in the development of a comprehensive UNDP Offer on RID that spans different risk management practices (i.e. DRR, CCA, conflict prevention, health/environmental risk, PVE). 

The UNDP Discussion Paper on the Governance of Systemic Risk was published as a contribution to the 2022 Global Assessment Report (GAR) on DRR. It also informed the implementation of UNDP&#x2019;s Strategic Plan and CB ongoing work on risk governance. It calls for UNDP to approach the governance of systemic risk not from a hazard specific practice, but from an integrated and multi-risk approach to strengthen national and local governance and resilience. 

Coordinated the development of a UNDP-wide Urban Resilience Strategy to help create a future where small and medium-sized cities in particular, and urban areas in general, are resilient to multiple risks and are safe, inclusive and prosperous places to live and work. City pilots to apply the strategy have commenced. 

The UNDP Strategy Tool for Integrating DRR and CCA into Development was finalized, in a joint effort that has been led by CB/DRT in collaboration with the NCE Team. This strategy tool addresses repeated calls for practical guidance on integrating both disaster and climate related risks into development, and an approach that helps overcome policy siloes for joined-up implementation and localization. It is now rolled out in selected UNDP programme countries.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
